<title>EGYPT: Yield rises on Egyptian three-month T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield rises on Egyptian three-month T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills rose to 9.999 percent from 9.991 percent at the previous auction on February 12.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: May 22, 1997 (May 15, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 9.999 percent (9.991)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 980.775 million (768.725 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1,055.825 million (884.225illion)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 9.800-10.091 percent (8.985-10.074)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 9.800-11.300 percent (8.985-10.183)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 127 (208)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 135 (221)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.40 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
